{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789209152,"nonce":"UKWafPCbhC0RB4oIKYsUmkmRgp0=","title":"The LLVM tier lowers Rethrow as a throw, so a rethrown exception gets a fresh stack","message":"air_emit.rs emit_air_terminator lowers AirTerminator::Throw and Rethrow both to hlp_throw. Cranelift picks throw_helper(is_rethrow) and the runtime differs: hlp_throw -\u003e throw_impl(v, true) re-captures the exception stack, hlp_rethrow -\u003e throw_impl(v, false) keeps it (std/src/error.rs). Observable through haxe.CallStack.exceptionStack() after a rethrow: the LLVM tier reports the rethrow site, the other tiers the original throw site.","files":null}]}